{"id":"dan-the-tribe-of","name":"Dan, The Tribe Of","aliases":["Dan"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:dan-the-tribe-of"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Dan","text":"A judge. (1.) The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni). The blessing pronounced on him by his father was, “Dan shall judge his people” (49:16), probably in allusion to the judgeship of Samson, who was of the tribe of Dan. The tribe of Dan had their place in the march through the wilderness on the north side of the tabernacle (Num. 2:25, 31; 10:25). It was the last of the tribes to receive a portion in the Land of Promise. Its position and extent are described in Josh. 19:40-48. The territory of Dan extended from the west of that of Ephraim and Benjamin to the sea. It was a small territory, but was very fertile. It included in it, among others, the cities of Lydda, Ekron, and Joppa, which formed its northern boundary. But this district was too limited. “Squeezed into the narrow strip between the mountains and the sea, …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1835","lemma":"דָּן","xlit":"Dân","gloss":"Dan, one of the sons of Jacob","kjv":"Daniel","count":24,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H6881","lemma":"צׇרְעָה","xlit":"Tsorʻâh","gloss":"Tsorah, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Zareah, Zorah, Zoreah","count":6,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H5996","lemma":"עַמִּישַׁדַּי","xlit":"ʻAmmîyshadday","gloss":"Ammishaddai, an Israelite","kjv":"Ammishaddai","count":5,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H1839","lemma":"דָּנִי","xlit":"Dânîy","gloss":"a Danite or descendants of Dan","kjv":"Danites, of Daniel","count":5,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H295","lemma":"אֲחִיעֶזֶר","xlit":"ʼĂchîyʻezer","gloss":"Achiezer, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Ahiezer","count":5,"share":0.09},{"strong":"H847","lemma":"אֶשְׁתָּאֹל","xlit":"ʼEshtâʼôl","gloss":"Eshtaol, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Eshtaol","count":5,"share":0.09}],"verses":["Gen.30.6","Gen.49.16","Gen.49.17